    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d538">

                <pb facs="0438" n="430" sameAs="frus:frus1937v04/pg430"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/9340: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-08-13T19:00:00+08:00">August 13, 1937—7
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received August 13—1:15 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>422. My 415, August 13, 8 a.m.,<anchor n="75" xml:id="d538-f1"/> second
                    paragraph, and 418, August 13, 3 p.m. The following is translation made by
                    Embassy of notification received from the Foreign Office date August 13.</p>
                <pb facs="0439" n="431" xml:id="pg431"/>
                <quote rend="blockquote">
                    <p>“I have the honor to inform you that in view of present compelling
                        circumstances the Chinese Government has closed the Yangtze River below
                        Chinkiang to navigation. All navigation on that section of the river is
                        therefore suspended. I have the honor to indite this formal note for your
                        information and to request that instructions be issued to American residents
                        uniformally [<hi rendition="#italic">sic</hi>] to take note”.<anchor n="76"
                            xml:id="d538-f2"/></p>
                </quote>
                <p>Nanking station vessel has been informed.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Peiping, Shanghai, Hankow.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d538-f1" n="75" xml:id="d538-f1-content">
                <p><ref target="frus1937v03#pg_392">Vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps">iii</hi>, p.
                        392</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d538-f2" n="76" xml:id="d538-f2-content">
                <p>On August 27 the Chinese Foreign Office replied to the American Embassy’s inquiry
                    of August 25 that the Yangtze would remain closed for the present to all
                    shipping (811.30 Asiatic Fleet/336).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
